9. **Stay in your lane.** Edit only inside your own workspace clone (`workspace/claude/commons-cli`). Don't commit, push or switch branches; `kit.py` does that. Don't open other LLMs' folders under `runs/` or `workspace/`. Don't edit the kit or the Excel files by hand, or anything in the run folder except `process.md`; `kit.py` writes them. You **are allowed** to run `python kit.py metrics --smell W04 --llm "<your LLM name>"` after your last `finish`: it measures size, cohesion and coupling before and after with CK and fills your run's row of the Excel **Metrics** sheet.


## 5. Definition of done

- `python kit.py test --llm "Claude"` shows the same number of passing tests as the original run (see `runs/claude/W04/tests_original.json`).
- No file under `src/test/` changed, and no public or protected API was removed or changed.
- The smell is addressed with the technique in section 2, and nothing else changed.
- `process.md` is complete: every _italic guidance line_ has been replaced.
- `python kit.py finish --smell W04 --llm "Claude"` has run and printed a verdict.

## 6. Commands

| Purpose | Command |
|---|---|
| Quick test (one class) | `python kit.py test --llm "Claude" --only HelpFormatterTest` |
| Full test suite | `python kit.py test --llm "Claude"` |
| Finish the run | `python kit.py finish --smell W04 --llm "Claude"` |

